      "problem": "$(8-\\sqrt{-4})-(-7+\\sqrt{-49})=$",
      "worked_solution": "Given the complex number $a+b\\,\\text{i},$ $a$ represents its real part while $b$ represents its imaginary part.\n\nTo add or subtract complex numbers, we add or subtract their real parts, and we add or subtract their imaginary parts.\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8-\\sqrt{-4})-(-7+\\sqrt{-49}) & =(8-2\\,\\text{i})-(-7+7\\,\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(8-(-7))+(-2-7)\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =(8+7)-9\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =15-9\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
